Match a payload variant to use its fields.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    Status = {
        Ready,
        Failed | message String = "unknown error" |,
    }

    status = Status::Failed()
    if status is {
        case Ready: io.line("ready")
        case Failed(message): io.line(message)
    }
]

The capture name matches the field name. Here it reads the default message.

Use `as` when the local name should be clearer:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    case Failed(message as error_text): io.line(error_text)
]

Payload values are immutable. Pattern matching reads them without exposing
direct field mutation.
